window.CalcPast["2024-2"] = {"year":"2024–2025","sitting":2,"kind":"Resit","date":"June 23, 2025","iso":"2025-06-23","minutes":120,"file":"calc-exam-2024-02","instructions":["You get 10 points for writing your name and student number on each page (the grade is (points + 10)/10).","For each item the maximum score is indicated; in total you can score 100 points.","A regular calculator is allowed; graphical/programmable calculators, phones and other devices are not.","You have 120 minutes (most students with extra time: 150 minutes).","Always explain your calculations. Do not write numbers in digits (e.g. 0.25) but use fractions (e.g. 1/4) and simplify as much as possible."],"questions":[{"no":"1","points":36,"intro":"Select the best fitting answer.","items":[{"label":"(a)","prompt":"A continuous random variable $X$ has the probability distribution $$g(x)=\\begin{cases}\\frac13\\lfloor x\\rfloor & \\text{if } 0\\le x\\le3\\\\ 0 & \\text{otherwise}\\end{cases}$$ with $\\lfloor x\\rfloor$ the floor function, i.e., returning the greatest integer less than or equal to $x$. Then the expected value of $X$ is","parts":[{"kind":"choice","label":"","options":["$\\frac13\\cdot\\frac92$","$\\frac13\\cdot5$","$\\frac13\\cdot\\frac{11}2$","$\\frac13\\cdot6$","$\\frac13\\cdot\\frac{13}2$"],"answer":4,"latex":"$\\frac13\\cdot\\frac{13}2$"}],"points":4,"topic":"continuous","hints":["Split $[0,3]$ into the pieces where $\\lfloor x\\rfloor$ is $0$, $1$ and $2$."],"solution":["$E = \\frac13\\left(\\int_1^2x\\,dx + \\int_2^3 2x\\,dx\\right) = \\frac13\\left(\\frac32 + 5\\right) = \\frac13\\cdot\\frac{13}2$. **(E)**"]},{"label":"(b)","prompt":"Let $f(x)=\\ln\\left(\\dfrac{e^x-1}{e^x+1}\\right)$, then its domain is","parts":[{"kind":"choice","label":"","options":["$\\mathbb{R}$","$(-\\infty,0]$","$[0,\\infty)$","none of the above"],"answer":3,"latex":"none of the above"}],"points":4,"topic":"domain-range","hints":["The argument of $\\ln$ must be $> 0$; $e^x + 1 > 0$ always."],"solution":["Need $e^x > 1$, i.e. $x > 0$: the domain is $(0,\\infty)$, not listed. **(D)**"]},{"label":"(c)","prompt":"Let $f(x)=\\ln\\left(\\dfrac{e^x-1}{e^x+1}\\right)$, then its inverse is","parts":[{"kind":"choice","label":"","options":["$\\ln\\left(\\frac{1-e^x}{e^x-1}\\right)$","$\\ln\\left(\\frac{1-e^x}{-e^x-1}\\right)$","$\\ln\\left(\\frac{-1-e^x}{-e^x-1}\\right)$","$\\ln\\left(\\frac{-e^x-1}{e^x-1}\\right)$"],"answer":3,"latex":"$\\ln\\left(\\frac{-e^x-1}{e^x-1}\\right)$"}],"points":4,"topic":"inverse","hints":["$e^y = \\frac{e^x-1}{e^x+1}$: solve for $e^x$."],"solution":["$e^y(e^x+1) = e^x - 1 \\Rightarrow e^x = \\frac{1+e^y}{1-e^y} = \\frac{-e^y-1}{e^y-1}$. **(D)**"]},{"label":"(d)","prompt":"If $f$ is a function that is neither odd nor even, doesn’t have a minimum or a maximum, and never takes negative values, then $f$ could be","parts":[{"kind":"choice","label":"","options":["$\\ln(x)$","$\\frac1{|x|}$","$e^{-x}$","$|\\ln(x)|$","none of the above"],"answer":2,"latex":"$e^{-x}$"}],"points":4,"topic":"even-odd","hints":["Check each property for each candidate."],"solution":["$\\ln x$ takes negative values; $\\frac1{|x|}$ is even; $|\\ln x|$ has a minimum at $1$. $e^{-x}$ satisfies everything. **(C)**"]},{"label":"(e)","prompt":"Let $f(x,y)=\\dfrac{x+y}{x-y}$. The second partial derivative $\\frac{\\partial^2f}{\\partial x\\partial y}$ is","parts":[{"kind":"choice","label":"","options":["$\\frac{-2x-2y}{(x-y)^3}$","$\\frac{2x+2y}{(x-y)^3}$","$\\frac{-2x+2y}{(x-y)^3}$","$\\frac{2x-2y}{(x-y)^3}$"],"answer":0,"latex":"$\\frac{-2x-2y}{(x-y)^3}$"}],"points":4,"topic":"partial-derivatives","hints":["Quotient rule for $f_y$, then again for $\\partial_x$."],"solution":["$f_y = \\frac{2x}{(x-y)^2}$; $\\partial_x$: $\\frac{2(x-y) - 4x}{(x-y)^3} = \\frac{-2x-2y}{(x-y)^3}$. **(A)**"]},{"label":"(f)","prompt":"Let $f(x)=x\\sqrt{x^2-1}$ and $g(x)=\\dfrac{\\tan x}{x}$. Then","parts":[{"kind":"choice","label":"","options":["$f$ is odd, and $g$ is odd","$f$ is odd, and $g$ is even","$f$ is even, and $g$ is odd","$f$ is even, and $g$ is even","one of them is neither odd nor even"],"answer":1,"latex":"$f$ is odd, and $g$ is even"}],"points":4,"topic":"even-odd","hints":["odd·even = odd; odd/odd = even."],"solution":["$f$: $x$ odd times $\\sqrt{x^2-1}$ even: odd. $g$: odd/odd: even. **(B)**"]},{"label":"(g)","prompt":"One of the slant asymptotes of $f(x)=\\sqrt{a+bx^2}$ for some $a,b\\in\\mathbb{N}$ is best described by:","parts":[{"kind":"choice","label":"","options":["$(a+b)x$","$-bx$","$\\sqrt{a-b}\\,x$","$\\sqrt{b}\\,x$","$f$ has no slant asymptotes"],"answer":3,"latex":"$\\sqrt{b}\\,x$"}],"points":4,"topic":"asymptotes","hints":["For large $|x|$, $\\sqrt{a + bx^2}\\approx\\sqrt b\\,|x|$."],"solution":["$\\lim\\frac{f(x)}{x} = \\sqrt b$ for $x\\to\\infty$ (and $b = \\lim(f - \\sqrt bx) = 0$): $y = \\sqrt b\\,x$. **(D)**"]},{"label":"(h)","prompt":"Suppose that three standard dice, with faces numbered from ‘1’ to ‘6’, are rolled together. What is the probability of getting at least one ‘4’ after the roll?","parts":[{"kind":"choice","label":"","options":["$\\frac{1}{216}$","$\\frac{15}{216}$","$\\frac{75}{216}$","$\\frac{91}{216}$","$\\frac{125}{216}$"],"answer":3,"latex":"$\\frac{91}{216}$"}],"points":4,"topic":"discrete","hints":["Complement: no ‘4’ at all."],"solution":["$1 - (\\frac56)^3 = 1 - \\frac{125}{216} = \\frac{91}{216}$. **(D)**"]},{"label":"(i)","prompt":"What is the value of the improper integral $\\int_0^\\infty(\\cos(x)-\\sin(x))\\,dx$?","parts":[{"kind":"choice","label":"","options":["$0$","$1$","$\\sqrt2$","$\\infty$","none of the above"],"answer":4,"latex":"none of the above"}],"points":4,"topic":"substitution","hints":["Find the antiderivative and look at its behaviour as $x\\to\\infty$."],"solution":["$\\int_0^R = \\sin R + \\cos R - 1$, which keeps oscillating: the improper integral does not exist. **(E)**"]}]},{"no":"2","points":6,"intro":"","items":[{"label":"","prompt":"Let $G$ be the graph of the implicit function $ax^2-ax^2y+y^2+b=0$ for some $a,b\\in\\mathbb{Z}$. Let $A=(1,3)$ be a point of $G$ with a tangent line having a $y$-intercept of $-1$. Determine the slope $m\\in\\mathbb{Z}$ of this tangent line.","parts":[{"kind":"number","label":"$m =$","answer":"4","latex":"4"}],"points":6,"topic":"implicit-tangent","hints":["Find $y'$ in terms of $a$ at $A$; the tangent $y - 3 = m(x - 1)$ must have intercept $-1$.","The answer is a positive integer."],"solution":["$2ax - 2axy - ax^2y' + 2yy' = 0 \\Rightarrow y' = \\dfrac{2ax(y-1)}{2y - ax^2}$; at $A$: $\\dfrac{4a}{6-a}$.","Intercept: $3 - \\frac{4a}{6-a} = -1 \\Rightarrow a = 3$ (and $b = -3$).","$m = \\frac{12}{3} = 4$."]}]},{"no":"3","points":6,"intro":"","items":[{"label":"","prompt":"Determine the following limit (in $\\mathbb{N}$) $$\\lim_{n\\to\\infty}e\\cdot\\prod_{r=1}^n\\left(\\left(1+\\left(\\frac rn\\right)^2\\right)^{\\frac{2r}{n^2}}\\right)$$","parts":[{"kind":"number","label":"Limit:","answer":"4","latex":"4"}],"points":6,"topic":"riemann","hints":["Take the logarithm of the product: it becomes $\\sum\\frac1n\\cdot2\\frac rn\\ln(1 + (\\frac rn)^2)$.","The answer is a positive integer."],"solution":["$\\ln L = \\lim\\sum\\frac1n\\cdot2\\frac rn\\ln\\left(1 + \\left(\\frac rn\\right)^2\\right) = \\int_0^1 2x\\ln(1+x^2)dx$.","$u = 1 + x^2$: $\\int_1^2\\ln u\\,du = [u\\ln u - u]_1^2 = 2\\ln2 - 1 = \\ln\\frac4e$.","$L = \\frac4e$, so the limit is $e\\cdot\\frac4e = 4$."]}]},{"no":"4","points":6,"intro":"","items":[{"label":"","prompt":"Let $A$ be the area enclosed by the three half circles • $y=\\sqrt{1-x^2}$, defined on the domain $x\\in[-1,1]$; • $y=\\sqrt{1-(x-1)^2}-1$, defined on the domain $x\\in[0,2]$; • $y=\\sqrt{1-(x+1)^2}-1$, defined on the domain $x\\in[-2,0]$. Determine the size of the area $A\\in\\mathbb{N}$. *NB: You can use integral calculations to determine the area between the curves, but these are not needed as there is also a more intuitive solution than only requires a careful examination of the curves.*","parts":[{"kind":"number","label":"$A =$","answer":"2","latex":"2"}],"points":6,"topic":"area","hints":["Sketch the three half circles. The parts below the $x$-axis exactly fill what is missing from a rectangle.","The answer is a positive integer."],"solution":["The region below the $x$-axis is exactly the part missing from the rectangle with corners $(-1,0)$ and $(1,1)$ above the axis.","So $A$ equals the area of that rectangle: $2$."]}]},{"no":"5","points":6,"intro":"","items":[{"label":"","prompt":"Let $f(x)=\\sqrt{\\left(\\dfrac{x^2-2}{x-2}\\right)e^x}$. Compute the derivative using **logarithmic derivation**.","parts":[{"kind":"expr","label":"$f'(x) =$","answer":"sqrt((x^2 - 2)/(x - 2))*(x/(x^2 - 2) + 1/2 - 1/(2*x - 4))*exp(x/2)","latex":"\\sqrt{\\frac{x^{2} - 2}{x - 2}} \\left(\\frac{x}{x^{2} - 2} + \\frac{1}{2} - \\frac{1}{2 x - 4}\\right) e^{\\frac{x}{2}}","vars":["x"],"sample":{"x":[2.3,4.0]}}],"points":6,"topic":"derivative-rules","hints":["$\\ln f = \\frac12\\left(\\ln(x^2-2) - \\ln(x-2) + x\\right)$; differentiate and multiply by $f$.","The answer contains $e$ and a root."],"solution":["$\\ln f = \\frac12\\big(\\ln(x^2-2) - \\ln(x-2) + x\\big)$ (the factor $e^x$ is inside the root).","$[\\ln f]^{\\prime} = \\frac{x}{x^2-2} - \\frac{1}{2(x-2)} + \\frac12$.","$f'(x) = \\sqrt{\\frac{x^2-2}{x-2}e^x}\\left(\\frac{x}{x^2-2} - \\frac{1}{2(x-2)} + \\frac12\\right)$."]}]},{"no":"6","points":6,"intro":"","items":[{"label":"","prompt":"Let $A,B,C\\in\\mathbb{Q}$ and $A,B,C>0$. Suppose that $$\\lim_{x\\to0}\\frac{(A\\cdot x+B)^3-8-C\\cdot\\sin(x)}{1-\\cos(x)}=3$$ Determine the values for $A$, $B$, $C$.","parts":[{"kind":"number","label":"$A =$","answer":"1/2","latex":"\\frac{1}{2}"},{"kind":"number","label":"$B =$","answer":"2","latex":"2"},{"kind":"number","label":"$C =$","answer":"6","latex":"6"}],"points":6,"topic":"lhopital","hints":["Denominator $\\to0$: numerator $\\to0$ gives $B$. After one L'Hôpital step the denominator $\\sin x\\to0$ again.","$A =$ The answer is a positive fraction (not an integer). $B =$ The answer is a positive integer. $C =$ The answer is a positive integer."],"solution":["$B^3 - 8 = 0 \\Rightarrow B = 2$.","L'Hôpital: $\\dfrac{3(Ax+B)^2A - C\\cos x}{\\sin x}$; numerator at $0$: $12A - C = 0$.","L'Hôpital: $\\dfrac{6(Ax+B)A^2 + C\\sin x}{\\cos x}\\to12A^2 = 3 \\Rightarrow A = \\frac12$, $C = 6$."]}]},{"no":"7","points":6,"intro":"","items":[{"label":"","prompt":"Determine $\\int\\sin(2x)e^{4x}dx$.","parts":[{"kind":"expr","label":"$\\displaystyle\\int\\sin(2x)e^{4x}dx =$","answer":"exp(4*x)*sin(2*x)/5 - exp(4*x)*cos(2*x)/10","latex":"\\frac{e^{4 x} \\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)}}{5} - \\frac{e^{4 x} \\cos{\\left(2 x \\right)}}{10} + C","vars":["x"],"sample":{"x":[-1.0,0.5]},"upToConstant":true}],"points":6,"topic":"by-parts","hints":["By parts twice (integrate $e^{4x}$ each time); the original integral comes back — solve for it.","The answer contains $e$ and a trigonometric function. Adding $+C$ is optional."],"solution":["$\\int\\sin(2x)e^{4x}dx = \\frac14\\sin(2x)e^{4x} - \\frac2{16}\\cos(2x)e^{4x} - \\frac14\\int\\sin(2x)e^{4x}dx$.","$\\frac54\\int\\sin(2x)e^{4x}dx = \\frac14\\sin(2x)e^{4x} - \\frac18\\cos(2x)e^{4x}$.","$\\int\\sin(2x)e^{4x}dx = \\frac15\\sin(2x)e^{4x} - \\frac1{10}\\cos(2x)e^{4x} + C$."]}]},{"no":"8","points":12,"intro":"Determine the following limits (in $\\mathbb{Z}$ when it exists) where $f$ and $g$ are defined by the following graphs [[img:assets/past-exams/2025-06-q8-f.png|Graph of y = f(x) on [-4, 4]]] [[img:assets/past-exams/2025-06-q8-g.png|Graph of y = g(x) on [-4, 4]]]","items":[{"label":"(i)","prompt":"$\\lim_{x\\to1}f(x)+g(x)$","parts":[{"kind":"number","label":"Limit:","answer":"2","latex":"2"}],"points":4,"topic":"limits","hints":["Compute both one-sided limits of $f$ and $g$ at $1$ separately and add them.","The answer is a positive integer."],"solution":["From the left: $1 + 1 = 2$; from the right: $4 + (-2) = 2$. The limit is $2$."]},{"label":"(ii)","prompt":"$\\lim_{x\\to-1}\\dfrac{f(x)}{g(x)}$","parts":[{"kind":"number","label":"Limit:","answer":"6","latex":"6"}],"points":4,"topic":"lhopital","hints":["$f(-1) = g(-1) = 0$: form $\\tfrac00$. Both are straight lines near $-1$ — compare their slopes.","The answer is a positive integer."],"solution":["Near $-1$: $f(x) = 3x + 3$ and $g(x) = \\frac12x + \\frac12$.","$\\lim\\frac{f}{g} = \\frac{f'}{g'} = \\frac{3}{1/2} = 6$."]},{"label":"(iii)","prompt":"$\\lim_{x\\to2}(f\\circ g)(x)$","parts":[{"kind":"number","label":"Limit:","answer":"-3","latex":"-3"}],"points":4,"topic":"limits","hints":["First find how $g(x)$ approaches its limit at $x = 2$ (from which side), then look at $f$ there.","The answer is a negative integer."],"solution":["As $x\\to2$, $g(x)\\to-2$ from above.","$\\lim_{y\\downarrow-2}f(y) = -3$."]}]},{"no":"9","points":6,"intro":"Consider a continuos random variable $X$ that takes values in the interval $[a,b]$ and has the following probability density function (pdf): $$p(x)=\\frac{Z}{(b-a)^3}\\left(x-\\frac{a+b}{2}\\right)^2$$ for $x\\in[a,b]$, $Z>0$. This is sometimes called the $U$-quadratic distribution.","items":[{"label":"(a)","prompt":"What is the value of $Z\\in\\mathbb{N}$, such that $p(x)$ is properly normalized?","parts":[{"kind":"number","label":"$Z =$","answer":"12","latex":"12"}],"points":2,"topic":"continuous","hints":["$\\int\\left(x - \\frac{a+b}2\\right)^2dx = \\frac13\\left(x - \\frac{a+b}2\\right)^3$.","The answer is a positive integer."],"solution":["$1 = \\frac{Z}{(b-a)^3}\\cdot\\frac13\\left[\\left(\\frac{b-a}2\\right)^3 - \\left(-\\frac{b-a}2\\right)^3\\right] = \\frac{Z}{(b-a)^3}\\cdot\\frac13\\cdot\\frac{(b-a)^3}{4} = \\frac{Z}{12}$.","$Z = 12$."]},{"label":"(b)","prompt":"Derive the **mean** and the **mode** of the above distribution, knowing that: • The mean is the expected value of the random variable, that is, $E(X)=\\int xp(x)dx$; • The mode conists of all the values of $X$ for which the pdf $p(x)$ obtains its maximum, in other words $\\arg\\max_{x\\in[a,b]}p(x)$.","parts":[{"kind":"expr","label":"Mean $=$","answer":"a/2 + b/2","latex":"\\frac{a}{2} + \\frac{b}{2}","vars":["a","b"],"sample":{"a":[0.0,1.0],"b":[2.0,4.0]},"points":2.0},{"kind":"set","label":"Mode (all values):","answer":["a","b"],"vars":["a","b"],"sample":{"a":[0.0,1.0],"b":[2.0,4.0]},"latex":"\\{a, b\\}","points":2.0}],"points":4,"topic":"continuous","hints":["The pdf is symmetric around $\\frac{a+b}2$; where is a upward parabola largest on a closed interval?","Mean $=$ The answer is an expression in $a, b$. Mode (all values): There are 2 values (they may depend on $a$, $b$)."],"solution":["Symmetry around $\\frac{a+b}2$ gives mean $\\frac{a+b}2$.","The parabola is maximal at both endpoints: mode $\\{a, b\\}$."]}]}],"id":"2024-2"};
